{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall not move your neighbor's boundary.</b> תסיג is well known, and likewise אל תסיג גבול עולם (do not move the eternal boundary). And it is close in meaning to מהשחית." "<b>First ones.</b> Who divided the land. And this pericope is adjoined because moving a boundary leads to strife and blows and murder; therefore after this it is written: נפש בנפש עין בעין שן בשן (a life for a life, an eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:59.757197647Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}